{"agent_id":"claude","agent_seq":39,"timestamp":"2026-06-21T00:30:02.524764549Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"93e3eec2-54b3-4011-8d61-c2b423fa0539","comment_uuid":"b5e4cd0d-a735-4757-ae96-1a9e4168f26c","display_id":254,"author":"claude","content":"Landed as DRAFT PR #1209 (https://github.com/openwpm/OpenWPM/pull/1209), branch fix/geckodriver-fifo-sigabrt, base master.\n\nFix: backed FirefoxLogInterceptor with a REGULAR FILE instead of a FIFO. Regular-file writes never raise EPIPE, so geckodriver can no longer be aborted by reader/teardown ordering — removes the SIGABRT-on-teardown failure mode entirely (not just narrowing the race).\n\nChanges (3 files):\n- selenium_firefox.py: tempfile.mkstemp instead of mktempfifo; interceptor tails the file and stops on an explicit threading.Event (stop()), draining remaining lines then unlinking; removed unused mktempfifo helper. daemon flag retained.\n- deploy_firefox.py: log_output -> regular file; return interceptor to caller.\n- browser_manager.py: run_impl finally-block calls webdriver_interceptor.stop() (after driver already quit/killed, so no write can race).\n\nVerification:\n- Deterministic OS-level proof: FIFO write after reader-close -> EPIPE; regular-file write after reader-close -> succeeds (root cause confirmed + fix removes it).\n- Session-driven direct-Selenium repro (geckodriver 0.37.0 / FF 152): regular-file interceptor -> geckodriver survives reader teardown mid-session, log lines captured, clean exit. The exact FIFO abort window is timing-finicky to trigger on demand; OS-level proof + structural argument cover correctness, full validation on CI.\n- pytest -m pyonly green; mypy clean on both deploy files; black/isort clean; pre-commit green.\n\nNote: deeper cause is upstream (geckodriver/Rust should treat broken-pipe-on-stdout as clean exit, not panic-to-abort) — flagged in PR for a separate Mozilla report. Closes #1208. Not merged; draft for human review.","created_at":"2026-06-21T00:30:02.521706452Z","kind":"note","signed_by":"SHA256:s7/xSWzYQxlilryCkQ+87ei/Tb4h7UF7S3hGGeMOxBg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxYoY2+ykEqIdJITiF+QWTxSzAQrzXLyHaApd+5sgGJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAt9dVmY+LG6YVdPpgpjXk9I276mHAYqaWSzvX1wHwmWE8WfybmTpAoJAxhkE/wk2R9AWEge24/aLqfQgXah72Bw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:s7/xSWzYQxlilryCkQ+87ei/Tb4h7UF7S3hGGeMOxBg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxYoY2+ykEqIdJITiF+QWTxSzAQrzXLyHaApd+5sgGJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQC9qx78cFoxbPuAI1WqYfpQ75YwxMSUBLGhhKfbiVUjzsTx95bTUvWCjBUB4zoFY3+GpvjQwKQ53CGXOrRaf9Q8="}
{"agent_id":"claude","agent_seq":40,"timestamp":"2026-06-21T00:55:04.281473622Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"93e3eec2-54b3-4011-8d61-c2b423fa0539","comment_uuid":"4188ec83-4b85-4da6-884d-4e097f7213e7","display_id":255,"author":"claude","content":"HATER REVIEW (read-only, draft #1209) — VERDICT: Acceptable. Crash fix is SOUND: regular file removes the EPIPE mechanism (not just the window); verified at OS level; both teardown paths (graceful os._exit + forced SIGKILL) covered; no surviving FIFO/stderr EPIPE path. BUT two real defects gate merge: (1 MAJOR) temp-file LEAK on every teardown — unlink now lives only in run()'s finally, which never runs under os._exit() (daemon thread, no join) or SIGKILL. Original unlinked on first log line, eagerly+unconditionally. Long crawls leak thousands of owpm_driver_*.log in /tmp. Fix: unlink-on-open (after writer opens line 155); anonymous inode carried by open fds, leak-proof on all paths, deletes the drain dance. (2 MAJOR) stop()+drain is unjoined dead code — nothing waits for the drain before process exit. Plus (MINOR) regular-file readline() fragments lines split across flushes/polls into 2 log lines (debug-fidelity regression); (MINOR) zero test coverage for FirefoxLogInterceptor. Recommend: adopt unlink-on-open, delete stop()/drain, add 1 pyonly test. Full writeup: /home/vringar/projects/OpenWPM/datadir/hater-1209.md","created_at":"2026-06-21T00:55:04.278545364Z","kind":"note","signed_by":"SHA256:s7/xSWzYQxlilryCkQ+87ei/Tb4h7UF7S3hGGeMOxBg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxYoY2+ykEqIdJITiF+QWTxSzAQrzXLyHaApd+5sgGJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAFaNHMJjq6JyvoVxhNbE5Wmz+esjLKj1Z2ACFFqtRpXOb9yhw5LfKshsveahPojFQesNWXU6Tg7XuFayF5EcBDw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:s7/xSWzYQxlilryCkQ+87ei/Tb4h7UF7S3hGGeMOxBg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxYoY2+ykEqIdJITiF+QWTxSzAQrzXLyHaApd+5sgGJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MT