{"agent_id":"claude","agent_seq":41,"timestamp":"2026-06-21T01:25:25.270455735Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"93e3eec2-54b3-4011-8d61-c2b423fa0539","comment_uuid":"44b375ee-0ede-49a8-a7a6-c2eabff0aa90","display_id":256,"author":"claude","content":"Applied the-hater's fixes to PR #1209 (force-updated draft).\n\n**Issue #1 + #2 (Majors) collapsed via unlink-on-open:**\n- `selenium_firefox.py`: `FirefoxLogInterceptor` now opens the read fd in `start()` (before the writer opens by path). Removed the `threading.Event`/`stop()`/drain machinery entirely (it was unjoined dead code — daemon thread, no `join()`, would never run before `os._exit()`).\n- `deploy_firefox.py`: keep a reference to the geckodriver log write handle, then `os.unlink()` the path immediately after opening it. Both fds carry the now-anonymous inode to process exit. Leak-proof on all paths (graceful os._exit(), SIGKILL, exception) with no teardown hook. Verified no `/tmp/owpm_driver_*.log` leak.\n- `browser_manager.py`: dropped the `webdriver_interceptor.stop()` call in `run_impl` finally; interceptor is now a self-cleaning daemon.\n\n**Issue #3 (Minor, line fragmentation):** fixed — the tail loop buffers partial `readline()` results until a newline, so a driver line split across flushes/polls is emitted as one log entry (not two).\n\n**Issue #4 (Minor, zero coverage):** added `test/test_selenium_firefox.py` (3 pyonly tests): lines reach the logger; temp file unlinked-but-readable-via-fd (no leak); split writes not fragmented.\n\n**Issue #5 (Nitpick):** addressed incidentally — the write handle now has an explicit reference (`driver_log_fh`).\n\n**Crash fix intact:** regular file, no surviving FIFO codepath.\n\n**Verification:** 3/3 pyonly tests green; mypy clean on the 3 touched files; black/isort clean; jj-precommit green. Commit message updated to describe the unlink-on-open approach (was stale re: the removed Event/drain).","created_at":"2026-06-21T01:25:25.267623104Z","kind":"note","signed_by":"SHA256:s7/xSWzYQxlilryCkQ+87ei/Tb4h7UF7S3hGGeMOxBg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxYoY2+ykEqIdJITiF+QWTxSzAQrzXLyHaApd+5sgGJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAUDKgeQSyUG0i/PoU1JPO3ugNhimYGHBL5VuBP1Q9PEzdY6uSCqK11xp5Yh0BiF8PA43gxeDj3fAvJIfWunJEAg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:s7/xSWzYQxlilryCkQ+87ei/Tb4h7UF7S3hGGeMOxBg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxYoY2+ykEqIdJITiF+QWTxSzAQrzXLyHaApd+5sgGJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCwrNwIOU5zwGLM/NIIkClo2MpUqtAvztwUU9eaTe2Xv4K68GE1zBDBJHUCTDeZPKs+TyQixGEqIsHbIjFUxtAE="}
{"agent_id":"claude","agent_seq":42,"timestamp":"2026-06-21T01:57:07.414230776Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"7a08777f-0a60-4c7d-ba39-f31b4d8efb4c","comment_uuid":"1133c34d-906e-42ab-a901-dc0a5038c455","display_id":257,"author":"claude","content":"PREMISE VERDICT: NO-OP (like #53). Recommend closing as not-reproducible-via-this-vector.\n\nEmpirically verified via direct-selenium repro (FF151 headless + geckodriver, the real getStackTrace/getOriginatingScriptContext/instrumentFunction logic from js-instruments.ts injected as inline <script> text exactly like content-scope.ts::insertScript does, instrumenting window.atob, called from page code incl. the mid-stack deepA->deepB->atob case #54 worries about).\n\nThe recorded call_stack contains ZERO moz-extension:// frames in every case. Because the legacy instrument runs as an inline DOM-inserted <script> in the PAGE world, ALL its frames -- including the instrument's own getStackTrace/getOriginatingScriptContext/wrapper frames -- are attributed to the PAGE document URL, not moz-extension://. Example captured call_stack (http page): 'deepB@http://127.0.0.1:8731/page.html:8:35 / deepA@...:7:28 / window.__run@...:9:3'. trace.slice(3) already drops exactly the 3 instrument frames, and even pre-slice the raw stack has no extension origin. Stealth's filterExtensionFrames would have nothing to strip -- same no-op as #53. Mid-stack re-entry tested explicitly; still page-only.\n\nFull analysis + quoted stacks: datadir/verify-54-premise.md","created_at":"2026-06-21T01:57:07.411066878Z","kind":"note","signed_by":"SHA256:s7/xSWzYQxlilryCkQ+87ei/Tb4h7UF7S3hGGeMOxBg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxYoY2+ykEqIdJITiF+QWTxSzAQrzXLyHaApd+5sgGJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA7RYzGIvuJ7hXfH3ubSxdRGMoLDag2sbBH60ooJoUXJe1yFyyzOpMQUA8DMrcbieZEHiREcqBgk2D61qZ06bAAQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:s7/xSWzYQxlilryCkQ+87ei/Tb4h7UF7S3hGGeMOxBg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxYoY2+ykEqIdJITiF+QWTxSzAQrzXLyHaApd+5sgGJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBN+ceCDruSeSQRRA9wGsqI0nGo+s0Noypjxjf1mlk7KZwLVfrRdX4V62Dqqm0+6TDmizLHsGnvXBsB9YUu/Hwg="}
{"agent_id":"claude","agent_seq":43,"timestamp":"2026-06-21T02:26:23.328038784Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ebe42c7e-a4f1-4d44-a97e-06e3103530f1","comment_uuid":"fd6a50cc-b6f0-4a9b-b3e8-2ac1d8de8664","display_id":258,"author":"claude","content":"## R29 proto-chain-flattening (sub-item iii): REPRODUCES, but de-pollution is TRADEOFF-BLOCKED — no PR\n\nDirect-selenium repro (managed firefox-bin + geckodriver, headless, no extension; injects the **real compiled** `getInstrumentJS` via `.toString()` exactly as `${getInstrumentJS}` does). Harness + full writeup: `datadir/r56-repro/`, `datadir/r56-protochain-flattening-verdict.md`.\n\n### Step 1 — artifact REPRODUCES\nInstrumenting `CanvasRenderingContext2D.prototype` with empty `propertiesToInstrument` (the default for a bare-string interface request, used by `collection_fingerprinting`) triggers the whole-chain flatten (`js-instruments.ts:74-86` + `:670-703` → leaf `defineProperty` at `:513`):\n- own-prop count **73 → 84** (+11)\n- **11 `Object.prototype` members became OWN props of the leaf**: `__defineGetter__`, `__defineSetter__`, `__lookupGetter__`, `__lookupSetter__`, `__proto__`, `hasOwnProperty`, `isPrototypeOf`, `propertyIsEnumerable`, `toLocaleString`, `toString`, `valueOf`\n- direct probe `Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(proto,\"hasOwnProperty\")`: **false → true**. Non-enumerable (so invisible to `for-in`) but visible to `getOwnPropertyNames`/`hasOwnProperty`/`Reflect.ownKeys` — which the detector uses.\n\n### Step 2 — the flatten is LOAD-BEARING; surgical de-pollution breaks capture\nThe flatten exists to capture **inherited** members. Proven: instrument `AnalyserNode` (chain `AnalyserNode→AudioNode→EventTarget→Object`); `connect` is native on `AudioNode.prototype` (inherited, not own on the leaf). After instrumenting, `hasOwn(AnalyserNode.prototype,\"connect\")` flips **false→true**, AND calling `analyser.connect(gain)` **logs** `{operation:\"call\", symbol:\"AnalyserNode.connect\"}` — captured *because* it was copied down to the leaf. `collection_fingerprinting` depends on this path for 11/14 entries.\n\nThe investigation's proposed fix (\"redefine inherited members on the owning prototype, not the leaf\") de-pollutes mechanically but **regresses attribution**. Empirically: instrument BOTH `AnalyserNode` and `GainNode` (sibling `AudioNode` subclasses), call `gain.connect(dest)` → currently logs **exactly once**, correctly `symbol:\"GainNode.connect\"` (each leaf has its OWN copy → independent per-interface attribution). Folding the wrapper onto `AudioNode.prototype` would instead (a) double-wrap across every subclass in the collection, or (b) attribute every subclass's `connect` to whichever interface registered first. Per-interface granularity is lost.\n\nThere is **no plain-JS wrapper placement** that is both reachable on the leaf's chain ahead of the owning prototype AND not an own-prop of the leaf — that own-prop *is* the pollution. Only the stealth architecture (privileged-side Xray/`exportFunction`, reading the receiver's interface name at call time) delivers leaf-attribution without copying down. That's exactly the legacy/stealth mutual-exclusion (#1187) / ADR-0001 territory.\n\n### Verdict\n- Sub-item **iii (flatten) is real and reproduces**, but for the legacy plain-JS-wrapper architecture **de-polluting it fundamentally trades off against per-interface inherited-member capture** — can't have both without stealth. Per the conservative guard, **no fix shipped** (a naive de-pollution would silently break capture `collection_fingerprinting` relies on).\n- The other R29 sub-items DON'T have this tradeoff and remain safe additive wins (native `toString` i, native arity ii, module-local helpers iv, constructor re-attach vi) — the genuine \"shared base layer.\" The flatten (iii) specifically is the one structurally tied to legacy's capture model.\n- Note the investigation's §3/§4 understate this for the *whole-interface (empty-props) case*: legacy's per-leaf copy-down is precisely what buys correct per-subclass attribution of inherited members. Worth a correction.","created_at":"2026-06-21T02:26:23.324879063Z","kind":"note","signed_by":"SHA256:s7/xSWzYQxlilryCkQ+87ei/Tb4h7UF7S3hGGeMOxBg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxYoY2+ykEqIdJITiF+QWTxSzAQrzXLyHaApd+5sgGJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABArBWNLs+tmHPEV3JlfrXYT8VOJ0MzXq+AdHSzgH2P/pLsErJHIpw4sGjqlvYdg6M9Ekexejq6rqW592e2JZRKAg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:s7/xSWzYQxlilryCkQ+87ei/Tb4h7UF7S3hGGeMOxBg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxYoY2+ykEqIdJITiF+QWTxSzAQrzXLyHaApd+5sgGJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFalBtlyIv54wwdWSWe7ljdtVtykk+qjTkP9Y2xOTjzmt0ErWvcFQibyn6nYbVNIwnc3qWfFxGvRPy8QJWoZEQY="}
