{"agent_id":"claude","agent_seq":47,"timestamp":"2026-06-21T04:24:59.772204228Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ebe42c7e-a4f1-4d44-a97e-06e3103530f1","comment_uuid":"f6eaaa0b-f253-4646-95d4-cc49aed9f99f","display_id":262,"author":"claude","content":"the-hater adversarial pass (empirical, direct-selenium FF152) on PR #1210: CONVERGED. Verified: (1) .length/.name descriptor shape is an EXACT match to native {writable:false,enumerable:false,configurable:true} — no new artifact; (2) guard test genuinely fails on a faithful revert (not tautological); (3) no capture regression, all instrumented calls still log; (4) edge cases (bound/async/named) copied verbatim, no throw. Residual data-property->accessor shape artifact on getter/setter sites is #54 (out of scope). Builder->Hater converged; awaiting Stefan's review/merge.","created_at":"2026-06-21T04:24:59.769085863Z","kind":"note","signed_by":"SHA256:s7/xSWzYQxlilryCkQ+87ei/Tb4h7UF7S3hGGeMOxBg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxYoY2+ykEqIdJITiF+QWTxSzAQrzXLyHaApd+5sgGJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAIewiziZfQhJhhQEhNzuLdGIxLruuUqh/I4M7xlA+NP+1GCp8AsLUoD1ceORodf/mAgmA26saS/Ov4Fv/1h0vAA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:s7/xSWzYQxlilryCkQ+87ei/Tb4h7UF7S3hGGeMOxBg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxYoY2+ykEqIdJITiF+QWTxSzAQrzXLyHaApd+5sgGJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHmQFrBNqiUFyoBUd0z2X8zIVNb0+kzBjhzqDhK7rvlLgO6hBufoGNUORdaq3l8kA95YlY5XsNfxMazkQUo+vw8="}
{"agent_id":"claude","agent_seq":48,"timestamp":"2026-06-21T05:05:29.329178848Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"9329f564-d673-4cee-affa-9cb999c05f1a","comment_uuid":"1a24d131-485a-41b3-9bce-785050fe29ac","display_id":263,"author":"claude","content":"EMPIRICALLY VERIFIED + TRADEOFF-BLOCKED (no-op). Did NOT ship a fix.\n\nMethod: direct selenium + geckodriver 0.37 + Firefox 152, headless, no extension. Inlined the REAL compiled getInstrumentJS into a page via .toString() (exactly as the ${getInstrumentJS} template does), instrumented CanvasRenderingContext2D.prototype.getImageData, probed the page-observable toString surface. Harness preserved in datadir/issue57-repro/; full writeup in datadir/issue57-toString-verdict.md.\n\nPREMISE CORRECTION: #57 says legacy \"mocks a wrapped function's toString so it returns [native code]\" at js-instruments.ts:442-453 and asks to harden that mock against recursive toString.toString(). On current master that premise is FALSE — lines 442-453 are the plain closure with NO toString mock. There is no override function to recurse into yet; the actual artifact is the RAW leak.\n\nREPRODUCED (control):\n- native getImageData.toString() => \"function getImageData() { [native code] }\"\n- wrapped getImageData.toString() => the wrapper's full JS body (logCall(...); func.apply(...))\n- Function.prototype.toString.call(wrapped) => same JS body (no own-toString to bypass)\n- Function.prototype.toString.toString() => UNCHANGED native. Legacy never touches Function.prototype.toString, so today there is ZERO second-order leak. Any spoof would ADD one.\n\nSo #57 reduces to: should we ADD a toString spoof to legacy and harden it? Measured both candidate fixes empirically:\n\nApproach A (per-wrapper own toString): closes wrapped.toString() but ADDS three tells — wrapped.toString.toString() leaks the spoof source; Function.prototype.toString.call(wrapped) leaks the JS body (trivial bypass); hasOwnProperty(\"toString\")===true (native methods have none). Strictly worse.\n\nApproach B (global Function.prototype.toString patch + WeakMap<wrapper,nativeSrc> + self-spoof, name/length spoofed): main realm looks perfect (name \"toString\", length 0, wrapped native, toString.toString() native, plain fns unaffected). BUT defeated by a one-line CROSS-REALM bypass:\n  iframe.contentWindow.Function.prototype.toString.call(wrapper) => \"function wrapper(){ ... }\" (JS body), hasNative=false.\nClosing that needs patching Function.prototype.toString in EVERY realm (every iframe incl. srcdoc/about:blank/dynamically-created, plus createHTMLDocument, Workers) — an open-ended hook treadmill — while the main-realm patched toString is itself a permanently-mutated non-native intrinsic (its own detection surface).\n\nVERDICT: net-negative, mirrors the #56 prototype-chain-flatten decision. The footprint (permanently mutating a core intrinsic) is paid without buying real protection (cross-realm read still wins). Recommendation: do NOT retrofit toString stealth onto the legacy plain-closure instrument; treat full toString/identity stealth as a property of the stealth instrument (Proxy/exportFunction, native all the way down by construction — no cross-realm treadmill). If minimal legacy hardening is ever wanted, scope+document it as \"main-realm best-effort, defeated cross-realm,\" not as closing the vector.\n\nWorkspace: zero source changes; no PR opened. Repro/verdict are gitignored scratch under datadir/.","created_at":"2026-06-21T05:05:29.324747608Z","kind":"decision","signed_by":"SHA256:s7/xSWzYQxlilryCkQ+87ei/Tb4h7UF7S3hGGeMOxBg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxYoY2+ykEqIdJITiF+QWTxSzAQrzXLyHaApd+5sgGJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAsFO+xVRmRmrb0XFULrCZma+vYM5dbNVadMhhVENUpjTXaKZ12fOxku3RHi4PqN9Yq0xZHq8U+D36VuntXzl2AA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:s7/xSWzYQxlilryCkQ+87ei/Tb4h7UF7S3hGGeMOxBg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxYoY2+ykEqIdJITiF+QWTxSzAQrzXLyHaApd+5sgGJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQELRcxxWlqZUGDGFfuswV4+nFwtprKbtWvEjsX/oiVe7fsjarlfTPd6l8zp+Lc8N+1c17gVxzM+FnD0gSsyKlgg="}
