{"agent_id":"claude","agent_seq":80,"timestamp":"2026-08-25T03:02:02.829574475Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"811909de-c6ba-43b1-a357-5bd97fedaa53","comment_uuid":"af0523b9-c816-4353-9a21-e4392f6e411e","author":"claude","content":"PHASE 1 LANDED — scaffolding only, everything opted out.\n\nANTI-DEFANG PROOF: test_js_instrument.py was 7 passed / 0 skipped before, and is 7 passed / 7 skipped after — same 7 test names, same wall clock. The 7 new entries are all [stealth] skips with enumerated reasons. test_stealth.py 104 passed. Baseline was captured from the pre-edit tree.\n\nThree enforced properties:\n- _check_calls comparison body is BYTE-IDENTICAL to its previous content (verified mechanically by diffing lines 31-44 against @-, not by eye). Only the row source moved, behind a new _js_rows() hook.\n- get_config asserts the transpile produced no untranslated members: an untranslated member DISQUALIFIES a class from stealth mode rather than licensing a smaller expected set.\n- Back-projection drops the stealth-only 'receiver' column and nothing else; any further normalization requires explicit sign-off, stated as a module-docstring contract.\n\nStealth is opt-in: STEALTH_UNSUPPORTED_REASON defaults non-None. All 7 classes carry a specific reason (D10 cookie gap / D12 no failure propagation / window.instrumentJS reliance). A skip is a documented gap, not a pass.\n\nREAL BUG FOUND while implementing (not anticipated by the plan): hoisting settings from a per-call literal into a shared class attribute is NOT semantics-neutral. clean_js_instrumentation_settings aliases the caller's property list into its output (js_instrumentation.py:155) and _merge_settings extends it in place (:77), so handing out the class attribute by reference would let one visit mutate what the next visit — and the other browser — sees. Guarded with deepcopy. No current config reaches that path, but it is one duplicate 'object' key away.\n\nPlan corrections: back-projector placed un