{"agent_id":"claude","agent_seq":81,"timestamp":"2026-08-25T04:27:37.110170002Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"811909de-c6ba-43b1-a357-5bd97fedaa53","comment_uuid":"8ced4d73-f696-4f16-b5d8-e99b3e0ab90d","author":"claude","content":"Closed the Phase 1 zero-coverage gap: added test/test_js_data_backprojector.py (9 pyonly tests, 0.03s), folded into the Phase 1 commit so the module ships with its own guard rails.\n\nThe tests assert the ABSENCE of transformation at least as hard as its presence, because 'almost a no-op' is the load-bearing property: every non-receiver column preserved byte-for-byte; caller rows not mutated; sqlite3.Row accepted (that is what db_utils actually returns, not dict); row order preserved; duplicate rows NOT collapsed (legacy assertions count occurrences, so collapsing would hide capture loss); idempotent on already-legacy-shaped rows; and STEALTH_ONLY_COLUMNS == ('receiver',) pinned so widening the drop list is a visible defang rather than a quiet edit.\n\nTwo of the three previously-uncovered pieces remain uncovered by construction (the stealth branch of get_config and transpile_cached) — those need a class to opt in, i.e. Phase 2, which is blocked on owner decisions.","created_at":"2026-08-25T04:27:37.104904614Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:s7/xSWzYQxlilryCkQ+87ei/Tb4h7UF7S3hGGeMOxBg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxYoY2+ykEqIdJITiF+QWTxSzAQrzXLyHaApd+5sgGJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAKObleIXR+3YvYoVu0nM1pV5T73QpL7I01T3VTj7J0ReJafE3bm3UgHeDI9iSzYZEtskuTRllsGo0EiiB1s5gDQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:s7/xSWzYQxlilryCkQ+87ei/Tb4h7UF7S3hGGeMOxBg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxYoY2+ykEqIdJITiF+QWTxSzAQrzXLyHaApd+5sgGJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHg38ECWQiSZIQfccuokN/L8p28VO91N+TVgjujVUAPMBmSCJfyz1S/oepPbvrLKKxnD1YUKqIY0Avrq19s4Sg8="}
