{"agent_id":"claude","agent_seq":84,"timestamp":"2026-08-25T09:18:46.597748Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"65d58730-47fd-4422-8ba6-c24e331aff08","comment_uuid":"06bb4745-97d2-4065-8fed-d264e39e2f58","author":"claude","content":"PR CLASSIFICATION CORRECTED — the earlier file-path heuristic ('does the diff touch a stealth/ path') was wrong and under-scoped the cohort. Full sweep of all ~30 open PR descriptions: datadir/open-pr-stealth-classification.md.\n\nThe stealth cohort is 7 PRs, not 2. The decisive evidence was NOT in the PR bodies — it is in .crosslink/issues.db, which links crosslink #53 -> PR #1207, #56 -> #1210/#1191, #57 -> cited by #1212. ADR-0001 exists only on the #1154 branch, and GH #1187 (closed by #1191) names the stealth ADR outright.\n\nCORE: #1154, #1206 (do-not-merge PoC).\nEVIDENCE (the experimental substantiation for legacy claims): #1191, #1210, #1213, #1212, #1207 — NONE merged, which is precisely why those legacy claims remain true on master.\nINTERACTS (collision risk, not stealth work): #1178 (config.py; 'callstack_instrument requires js_instrument'), #1101 (replaces the browser_params.json path stealth config rides on), #1144, #1170, #1175, #526.\n\nACTION TAKEN: rebased and pushed all five EVIDENCE branches onto master 61d285fc (v0.36.0/FF154). All five rebased cleanly, zero conflicts. This matters beyond tidiness: a RED proof is only as good as the master it is proven against, and all five were proven against a pre-FF154 master.\n\nTWO FINDINGS THAT CHANGE THE GUIDE:\n1. #1207 substantiates NOTHING. Its body claims a cleanErrorStack back-port but the diff is test-only (grep -c cleanErrorStack = 0) and its own docstring concedes the assertion 'holds by construction'. #1212 shows it is vacuous. It is superseded/corrected by #1212, and crosslink #53, which it claims to close, is not addressed by its diff.\n2. Firefox-version incoherence a rebase cannot fix: #1210/#1212 were verified on FF152, #1183/#1184/#1189 on FF150, and #1154's own legacy_detectable ratchet was originally set from an FF150 run — all against an FF154 master. (The #1154 ratchet has since been re-verified on FF154; the others have not.) #1189 is worse than stale: its 'prime with N-1' premise is two majors obsolete.\n\nBLOCKED MERGEABLE WORK: #1191 is MERGEABLE, non-draft, zero capture cost (implementations moved to closure locals, byte-for-byte unchanged), RED-proven, and fixes the most damning config-independent OpenWPM tell that EVERY current legacy user ships — and it needs nothing from stealth. #1210 same argument. Both are sitting idle behind the stealth stack. #526 should be closed as superseded by #1154's D1 requirement (it is 508 commits behind), not rebased.","created_at":"2026-08-25T09:18:46.592703788Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:s7/xSWzYQxlilryCkQ+87ei/Tb4h7UF7S3hGGeMOxBg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxYoY2+ykEqIdJITiF+QWTxSzAQrzXLyHaApd+5sgGJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA/MQLC+wUQhn2RHTtn3cnLtpRiertHgOeyYqN0/+B/WaFO6f3/xaSWhuod/ftnpRugEMuc+L6N0Ecf704RiGNBw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:s7/xSWzYQxlilryCkQ+87ei/Tb4h7UF7S3hGGeMOxBg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxYoY2+ykEqIdJITiF+QWTxSzAQrzXLyHaApd+5sgGJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOJX4cnAW4rg4XU4SuZREBOq3tMCzMgB6bGSaIGaeSc/ExlqUMioCx5+WDTpfLNHqzpbCoyXfjydQX3VwLXPGQQ="}
{"agent_id":"claude","agent_seq":85,"timestamp":"2026-08-25T09:38:11.262531909Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"e6cdfcc9-6e79-44ed-84ad-200850487582","comment_uuid":"f76294b6-612a-42a6-a36f-0909d3d9421b","author":"claude","content":"EXPERIMENT RUN. VERDICT: the claim is half true, and the persuasive half is FALSE.\n\n- 'stealth stamp == baseline': CONFIRMED. Identical on all 42 built-in components plus 4 reproducible extra probes, visitorId included.\n- 'legacy stamp != baseline': REFUTED. Legacy is ALSO byte-identical to baseline on every reproducible probe. All four runs produced visitorId adb59d565c781837fa88a1929fcd66fe. There is no component on which legacy differs from baseline.\n\nNOT a dead experiment — the activity control proves both instruments were live and watching FingerprintJS compute its stamp: baseline 0 rows/0 symbols; stealth 124 rows/46 symbols; legacy 92 rows/39 symbols, including CanvasRenderingContext2D.fillText, HTMLCanvasElement.toDataURL, OscillatorNode.start, window.navigator.*, window.screen.*, window.{local,session}Storage.\n\nWHY legacy is invisible is a property of the ORACLE, not the instrument. FingerprintJS OSS reads values, and OpenWPM's legacy wrappers are value-transparent. The bundle has exactly ONE isFunctionNative call site, guarding window.print inside a Safari-detection helper Gecko never reaches; it performs no integrity check on any instrumented surface. The vectors that DO expose legacy (Function.prototype.toString on wrapped natives, prototype shape, arity/name drift) are bot-detection vectors, and FingerprintJS OSS is not a bot detector.\n\nCONSEQUENCE: stop citing FingerprintJS for the legacy half — it does not support it, and the '27/28 components' claim in the guide and the #1154 PR body was not merely unsourced but wrong in direction. The correct evidence for the legacy half is test_stealth.py::TestStealthDetectability (8 legacy vectors failing on this same FF154 build). Honest framing that the data supports: stealth is invisible to a commodity fingerprinter, AND additionally invisible to the tamper vectors that expose legacy.\n\nVALIDITY GATE: baseline ran twice first; all 42 built-in components and visitorId stable. Excluded 2 probes (both halves of the forced-render canvas) after a control run entirely OUTSIDE OpenWPM (bare Selenium, plain FF154, no extension) showed Firefox re-seeds canvas noise PER PROFILE — 3 loads in one profile byte-identical, 2 fresh profiles differ, under stock prefs with fingerprintingProtection/resistFingerprinting/randomization all false and a -CanvasRandomization override. OpenWPM gives every launch a fresh profile; no pref pins it.\n\nBUG CAUGHT MID-FLIGHT: FingerprintJS v5's stabilized canvas source deliberately returns {geometry:skipped,text:skipped} on Firefox 120+. Canvas is the most heavily instrumented surface in the preset, so run #2 would have reported a vacuous canvas comparison. A forced-render probe via the library's own getUnstableCanvasFingerprint(false) export surfaced the per-profile randomization above.\n\nDELIVERED: test/test_pages/vendor/fingerprintjs-5.2.0.umd.min.js (byte-identical to npm, SHA-256 a8de5ead580c42d2e2b01a5752aa08da510852230971aa18554d67cd5de5775b, MIT, hash asserted in-test, monitoring:false to suppress the 1-in-1000 XHR to m1.openfpcdn.io), test/test_pages/fingerprintjs_stamp.html, test/test_fingerprintjs_stamp.py (6 tests, ~100s, 4 browser launches). 6/6 pass, 276 tests still collect, jj-precommit green.\n\nKNOWN HOLE: canvas image data is unmeasurable in this environment because of the per-profile randomization. If legacy leaks into rendered canvas bytes, this experiment could not see it.","created_at":"2026-08-25T09:38:11.256707186Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:s7/xSWzYQxlilryCkQ+87ei/Tb4h7UF7S3hGGeMOxBg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxYoY2+ykEqIdJITiF+QWTxSzAQrzXLyHaApd+5sgGJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAVdDxCzQMR166zFJh//z7m1stajp7/Vpfo/uHZJTzd2dFsexayi6BYBIctrtUtJhfRcHpFTRFsw+PB4PJUm1tBw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:s7/xSWzYQxlilryCkQ+87ei/Tb4h7UF7S3hGGeMOxBg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxYoY2+ykEqIdJITiF+QWTxSzAQrzXLyHaApd+5sgGJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJIexCzYl1AVQCfKNM5fulNeTtwhabKDV7j/dr2YCK8jn5x1vVeyXlgU5IuzzKBYhHy8xqp6HE35v6NjMjfXWAk="}
