{"agent_id":"claude","agent_seq":93,"timestamp":"2026-09-06T09:25:26.238833341Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"7cbf88ba-b84b-4b0b-9459-7d96f4bfd9bb","comment_uuid":"df42a3f9-3f39-49f1-9b6c-1a84404bff06","author":"claude","content":"Blocks the v0.37.0 release. Firefox 155.0.1 loads the extension, then its\nstartup JS throws before `extension_port.txt` is written, so every browser\nspawn fails with `Browser Ready: False` and the crawl retries until the\nfailure budget is exhausted.\n\n## Controlled experiment\n\nSame code, same machine, only the Firefox binary swapped:\n\n| Firefox | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| 154.0 (`9ce1ee6b`) | 2 browsers launched, 3 command sequences completed, clean shutdown |\n| 155.0.1 (`5fdfd009`) | 9 consecutive spawn failures, both browsers, every retry |\n\n```\nOpenWPM Firefox extension loaded\ndriver: JavaScript error: undefined, line 0: Error: An unexpected error occurred\nLooking for extension port information in .../firefox_profile_y_8eicy3\nFileNotFoundError: .../firefox_profile_y_8eicy3/extension_port.txt\n```\n\n## Not the harness\n\nReproduces with `web-ext` against the raw `bundled/` directory — no OpenWPM,\nno Selenium, no geckodriver:\n\n```\ncd Extension\nMOZ_HEADLESS=1 npx web-ext run --firefox=../firefox-bin/firefox \\\n  --source-dir=./bundled --no-reload --start-url=about:blank --verbose\n```\n\n## Bisect\n\nRemoving `experiment_apis` entries from `bundled/manifest.json` and counting\noccurrences of the error:\n\n| APIs declared | Error |\n| --- | --- |\n| all three | yes |\n| sockets + profileDirIO | yes |\n| sockets + stackDump | no |\n| profileDirIO + stackDump | no |\n| any single one | no |\n| none | no |\n\nSo it needs `sockets` *and* `profileDirIO`. That is consistent with the\nbackground script needing both to reach the actual failing call rather than\nwith either API being independently broken: `feature.js` opens the socket and\nthen calls `profileDirIO.writeFile(\"extension_port.txt\", ...)`, which is\nexactly the step that never completes.\n\n## Leading hypothesis (unconfirmed)\n\nFirefox 155 tightened `PathUtils.join` to reject empty components. Firefox's\nown code tripped it in the same session:\n\n```\nJavaScript error: resource:///modules/backup/BackupService.sys.mjs, line 4429:\nNotAllowedError: PathUtils.join: PathUtils does not support empty paths\n```\n\n`profileDirIO/api.js` builds its path with\n`PathUtils.join(PathUtils.profileDir, filename)`. If `PathUtils.profileDir` is\nempty in the experiment-API parent scope under 155, that throws.\n\nNot confirmed: the thrown error carries no file or line, and\n`extensions.logging.enabled` did not surface a stack.\n\n## Ruled out\n\n- Removing the legacy `Cu.importGlobalProperties` calls from\n  `profileDirIO/api.js` and `sockets/api.js` (the error string matches\n  `NS_ERROR_UNEXPECTED`). No effect; reverted.\n- The OpenWPM harness, per the `web-ext` reproduction above.\n- Rewriting `manifest.json` through `json.dump` — controlled for, still fails.\n\n## Next diagnostics\n\nNeeds an interactive session; this is poor territory for an agent.\n\n1. Attach the Browser Toolbox to a 155 instance and read the real stack.\n2. Log `PathUtils.profileDir` from inside the experiment API parent scope.\n3. Wrap the `profileDirIO` API body in try/catch and `Cu.reportError` the\n   caught value to get source info.\n4. Check the Firefox 154 -> 155 changelog for `PathUtils` / WebExtension\n   experiments changes.\n\n## Release impact\n\nv0.37.0 is on hold. The alternative discussed was shipping v0.36.1 without the\nFirefox bump (domain-utils 0.8.0, dependency refresh, Read the Docs fix); we\nchose to hold and fix instead.","created_at":"2026-09-06T09:25:26.233589953Z","kind":"note","signed_by":"SHA256:s7/xSWzYQxlilryCkQ+87ei/Tb4h7UF7S3hGGeMOxBg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxYoY2+ykEqIdJITiF+QWTxSzAQrzXLyHaApd+5sgGJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAnColJRr2iXhxWg3+thJSGVKGGgR5NM1Q8odiWgbC3ijjLwZgFaxVRJFwmYL9RZGB8MLCN+HSUrVdE3VsCVU+Cw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:s7/xSWzYQxlilryCkQ+87ei/Tb4h7UF7S3hGGeMOxBg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxYoY2+ykEqIdJITiF+QWTxSzAQrzXLyHaApd+5sgGJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQK5oOIaNobL51I1NXrhq/uFDHRqhAIcjw6AGyyGKUHPGZ0YGB1/9KD0gf4eONHegH/x3wk6PfeNiYa2A2EwMLAo="}
{"agent_id":"claude","agent_seq":94,"timestamp":"2026-09-06T10:33:29.415568205Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"7cbf88ba-b84b-4b0b-9459-7d96f4bfd9bb","comment_uuid":"f4fc4abd-9b21-44d3-97e2-ac3850b47bbc","author":"claude","content":"## Root cause found and fixed\n\nFirefox 155 rewrote `CheckAllowedURI` in\n`js/xpconnect/loader/mozJSSubScriptLoader.cpp`. Diffed against the 155.0.1 and\n154.0 release revisions:\n\n```cpp\n// 154 — file:/jar:/moz-extension: unconditionally allowed\nstatic bool CheckAllowedURI(JSContext* aCx, nsIURI* aURI) {\n  if (nsContentSecurityUtils::IsTrustedScheme(aURI)) return true;\n  // TODO(Bug 1974213) Block file: and jar: schemes.\n  // TODO(Bug 1976115) experiment_apis scripts are run from jar:file: URL\n  if (aURI->SchemeIs(\"file\") || aURI->SchemeIs(\"jar\")) return true;\n  if (aURI->SchemeIs(\"moz-extension\")) return true;\n  ReportError(aCx, \"Trying to load untrusted URI.\", aURI);\n\n// 155 — the same schemes now require an opt-in\nstatic bool CheckAllowedURI(JSContext* aCx, bool aAllowUnsafe, nsIURI* aURI) {\n  if (nsContentSecurityUtils::IsTrustedScheme(aURI)) return true;\n  if (aAllowUnsafe || StaticPrefs::security_allow_unsafe_subscript_loads()) {\n    if (aURI->SchemeIs(\"file\") || aURI->SchemeIs(\"jar\")) return true;\n    if (aURI->SchemeIs(\"moz-extension\")) return true;\n  }\n  ReportError(aCx, \"Trying to load untrusted URI.\", aURI);\n```\n\nMozilla's own comment names this exact case: *\"Bug 1976115 experiment_apis\nscripts are run from jar:file: URL instead of moz-extension:-URL\"*. OpenWPM\ninstalls a packed XPI, so the privileged API scripts under\n`Extension/bundled/privileged` load from a `jar:file:` URL and are now refused.\n\n`security.allow_unsafe_subscript_loads` is the only consumer of that pref in\nthe tree, and it is the documented escape hatch.\n\n## Fix\n\n`fo.set_preference(\"security.allow_unsafe_subscript_loads\", True)` in\n`openwpm/deploy_browsers/deploy_firefox.py`.\n\n## Validation\n\nA/B in the same tree, one line apart, Firefox 155.0.1:\n\n| pref | demo.py | command sequences | port writes | FileNotFoundError |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| set | exit 0 | 3 | 4 | 0 |\n| removed | exit 1 | 0 | 0 | 4 |\n\n## Retraction\n\nThe `web-ext` bisect in the previous comment is void. Those runs were all\nperformed while an experimental edit of mine (removing\n`Cu.importGlobalProperties` from the two API scripts) was still in the working\ntree, so they measured that edit, not the bug. After reverting it,\n`--source-dir` runs are clean with and without the pref — unpacked temporary\nextensions load from `moz-extension:`, not `jar:file:`, and did not reproduce.\n\nSpecifically withdrawn:\n\n- \"needs `sockets` and `profileDirIO` together\" — an artifact of the edit.\n- \"reproduces outside OpenWPM via web-ext\" — it did not, once the tree was clean.\n\nAlso withdrawn from that comment: the `PathUtils` empty-path hypothesis.\n`xpcom/ioutils/PathUtils.cpp` and `dom/chrome-webidl/PathUtils.webidl` are\nbyte-identical between 154 and 155, so the `BackupService` error was unrelated\nnoise. Profile-directory access did not change: `PathUtils.profileDir` and\n`PathUtils.getProfileDir()` are unchanged, and `PathUtils` is still injected\ninto the experiment-API sandbox global by `ExtensionCommon._createExtGlobal`.\n\n## Open question\n\n`ExtensionCommon.sys.mjs` line 1702 already passes `allowUnsafeURL: true` when\nloading API modules, which should have covered us without the pref. Line 1889\n(`loadScript`, for built-in `ext-*.js`) was not updated, but those use trusted\nschemes. Which path an XPI-packed experiment API actually takes is not yet\nestablished. Worth resolving before deciding whether the pref is a permanent\nfix or a workaround pending bug 1976115.","created_at":"2026-09-06T10:33:29.404178891Z","kind":"note","signed_by":"SHA256:s7/xSWzYQxlilryCkQ+87ei/Tb4h7UF7S3hGGeMOxBg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxYoY2+ykEqIdJITiF+QWTxSzAQrzXLyHaApd+5sgGJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABADBYSVlvEg5egywJgLWwjjEJAFS/VwmyUzVkYYOc/ho9AD3yDZu7h9/D70TU2wxgbsaDUf7qE5zLTxs/YsbaqBA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:s7/xSWzYQxlilryCkQ+87ei/Tb4h7UF7S3hGGeMOxBg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxYoY2+ykEqIdJITiF+QWTxSzAQrzXLyHaApd+5sgGJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNZ3Ca2OJ8Bs6ULGfD/WI+sQPpDkiRD+bt4S5JJeVyZZmupi/w561m1nIBHGbpeJ2YcN3umeCuMW69+wBdFjfAI="}
{"agent_id":"claude","agent_seq":95,"timestamp":"2026-09-06T14:08:45.568700917Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"7cbf88ba-b84b-4b0b-9459-7d96f4bfd9bb","comment_uuid":"b4025eee-72b2-45c9-9db0-a215106378a6","author":"claude","content":"Corrected bug attribution after checking Bugzilla directly.\n\nThe breaking change is bug 1974213 — \"Don't allow file: and jar: schemes in Services.scriptloader.loadSubScript\" — RESOLVED/FIXED, shipped in Firefox 155. That is what rewrote CheckAllowedURI and refused our jar:file: experiment API scripts.\n\nBug 1976115 — \"experiment_apis scripts are run from jar:file: URL instead of moz-extension:-URL\" — is NEW and tracks moving those scripts to a scheme that needs no opt-in. Once it lands, the security.allow_unsafe_subscript_loads pref can be dropped.\n\nBug 1974691 — \"Don't load subscripts from un-privileged moz-extension:\" — is NEW and would tighten the remaining scheme in the same function. This area is still in motion upstream, so CheckAllowedURI is worth re-checking at each Firefox bump.\n\nEarlier comments referred to 1976115 as though it were the cause; it is the tracking bug for the fix, not the regression.\n\nFix shipped in PR #1227, full CI green including the 7-way test matrix on Firefox 155.0.1.\n\nObsolete branch fix/tldextract-cache-race removed (local-only, never pushed, no PR). Its commit remains recoverable at change kovvwntpsmwqopolxxwrkytorvmrykuu / 1b08a187 if the workaround is ever wanted again.","created_at":"2026-09-06T14:08:45.563326429Z","kind":"note","signed_by":"SHA256:s7/xSWzYQxlilryCkQ+87ei/Tb4h7UF7S3hGGeMOxBg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxYoY2+ykEqIdJITiF+QWTxSzAQrzXLyHaApd+5sgGJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAosDC4dbX3Gs/0jizV6JAAKYKDJMxzqq9htMmAbv07zALIQEw7cyupBayWdBOF29sOujASGu7lcSrDwNGnZetBA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:s7/xSWzYQxlilryCkQ+87ei/Tb4h7UF7S3hGGeMOxBg","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgxYoY2+ykEqIdJITiF+QWTxSzAQrzXLyHaApd+5sgGJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQECkThcE7SQlH35K3yiEdbZoyW7/8rvpOgbT83G3+qWM/6JQ5kStEsjQgtniBmV85Ffp0qniaDNPPouWPmNjzAk="}
